 saw  the co-op row helping our main tarnish  man fighting off a boss earlier the  co-op bro actually used a similar  technique while helping battle against  this boss earlier in the trailer so that  means one of three things either a this  technique of using a dragon's power is  somewhat common and an ability you can  gain somewhere else in the game  b an ability you gain for defeating  godric or around where godric is or c  related to the earth tree that can be  seen near or within stormvale this is  what led me to think perhaps these  archerys could grant the player  abilities such as utilizing the same  dragon arm technique that godric uses  okay so gameplay out of the way let's  talk about some npcs npc number one is  alexander the iron fist he completely  gives off sigmar vibes or seek word if  you prefer dark souls 3. this friendly  npc seems to be one of the inhuman  enemies you come across and if that  definitely is the case and it's not just  some super elaborate outfit it means you  might have to be a little more careful  when attacking enemies as to not  accidentally attack a friendly npc  another major one is melina who could be  our new emerald herald slash maiden and  black etc etc she has an interesting  tattoo or scar along her left eye but  it's hard to say what this means just  yet she tells the player i  offer you an accord so it could be we  need her to level up and you offer her  runes in order to do so  within stormville there are two npcs we  encounter one who offers friendly advice  you can either take or ignore and rajet  who states this place is bristling with  tarnish hunters you know  they sacrifice our kind  for grafting there are a couple other  npcs that tarnish seems to run past but  doesn't speak within this trailer so i  just wanted to point these instances out  we also get to see the full cutscene  shown briefly in the gameplay trailer of  godric the golden ruler of stormville  godric refers to a dragon as the true  born heir perhaps of the elden ring as  well as someone kindred so it'll be  interesting to see what this actually  means and how it plays out when we can  truly dive into the lore  so there you have a breakdown of the  alden ring gameplay preview i hope i was  able to point out some things you missed  and if there were any cool details i  missed please do share as i mentioned i  previously did a video on everything we  know so far four months ago so there may  have been some details i didn't discuss  here that i did in that video thanks so  much for watching and i hope you enjoyed  and i'll see you guys soon for more  elden ring  you
 

